  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-152013",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed (I.I.D) normal random variables, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen \n\n$$\nY={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{n}∼N(n\\mu ,\\,n{\\sigma }^{2}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16}$ are independent and identically distributed, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{16} & ∼N(16\\cdot 0.5,\\,16\\cdot {0.3}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(16\\cdot 0.5,\\,16\\cdot 0.09) \\\\  & =N(8,1.44).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to compute the probability $P(8\\le Y\\le 9).$ We first convert $Y$ into a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(8\\le Y\\le 9) & =P(\\frac{8-8}{\\sqrt{1.44}}\\le Z\\le \\frac{9-8}{\\sqrt{1.44}}) \\\\  & =P(\\frac{0}{1.2}\\le Z\\le \\frac{1}{1.2}) \\\\  & =P(0\\le Z\\le 0.83) \\\\  & =Φ(0.83)-Φ(0) \\\\  & =Φ(0.83)-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.83)=0.7967\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(8\\le Y\\le 9) & =Φ(0.83)-0.5 \\\\  & =0.7967-0.5 \\\\  & =0.2967.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
